Description: SSH3 server - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 transport
 SSH3 server daemon: the SSH3 protocol carried over HTTP/3 (QUIC),
 implemented in C17 in the nginx style on top of the OpenSSL QUIC TLS
 API (the system libssl3t64, 3.5+).
 .
 The UDP/443 QUIC listener is socket-activated: systemd binds the
 datagram socket as root and hands the ready fd to the service
 (sd_listen_fds), so the service needs no CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE and
 comes up on the first packet.
 .
 System accounts authenticate out of the box: the password login
 rides on by default (the sshd PasswordAuthentication canon) and the
 root account never passes the Basic step.  Bearer JWT public keys,
 OIDC id_tokens, sessions, port forwarding and the in-process sftp
 with a chroot jail are also supported.
 .
 The daemon is configured through command-line flags (ssh3-server
 --help) and environment variables read from the conffile
 /etc/ssh3/ssh3-server.env (SSH3_LOG_LEVEL, SSH3_LOG_FILE,
 SSH3_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN, SSH3_ENABLE_PASSWORD_LOGIN).  See
 ssh3-server(8).
